@startuml
title Active Resource State Machine
[*] --> PROVISIONING : first Provision()
PROVISIONING --> READY : valid outputs persisted
READY --> PROVISIONING : later deployment reconcile
READY --> UNREFERENCED : absent from desired graph
UNREFERENCED --> PROVISIONING : referenced again
PROVISIONING --> FAILED : executor/output validation error
FAILED --> PROVISIONING : bounded known-transient retry
FAILED --> [*] : safe failure; interruption held in instance metadata
UNREFERENCED --> DESTROYING : confirmed PE/Admin scope or authorized run cleanup
DESTROYING --> DESTROYED : physical absence verified; keep audit
DESTROYING --> UNREFERENCED : failed known cleanup; retain operation/remaining IDs
DESTROYED --> [*]
note right of UNREFERENCED
  No destroy on workload removal.
V2 separate cleanup checks ownership/consumers.
  Environment-owned READY resources only;
  mark with successful current-set commit.
  Application-wide resources require
  cross-Environment ownership evidence.
end note
@enduml
